{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles","id":956545,"title":"[Open Call] The Mythos Chronicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-23T14:22:36-07:00","id":956545,"title":"[Open Call] The Mythos Chronicles","content":"<img src=\"http://maltedmeeple.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/CallofCthulhu.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Having just picked up the 7th Edition of Call of Cthulhu and being inundated with a Mythos Adventure Path in Pathfinder, I got myself thinking, where do the Mythos fit in Chronicles of Darkness?<br /> <br /> This thread has two goals.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Brainstorm plots, ideas, hooks, monsters and NPCs for a Mythos-themed CofD game.</li> <li>Develop a Dark Era based off of the 1920s that incorporate said themes. I would say that the primary regional focus of such an era would be the Northwest Atlantic (aka Lovecraft Country) but that it would also include events worldwide. Mythos Characters are surprising well-heeled travellers.</li> </ol><br /> <b>Historical Themes in the 1920s </b><ul><li>American Isolation</li> <li>Prohibition and moral temperance</li> <li>Rise of the Mob</li> <li>Boom Days of Pulp Magazines</li> </ul><b>Where do the Mythos fit? </b><br /> The short, flippant answer is probably everywhere. Every realm in the Chronicles of Darkness has the potential for creatures from the Cthulhu Mythos to appear. That being said, I think some realms are more appropriate than others. For the most part, the Supernal may play host to entities that are Cthulhian Cosmic Horrors, but they don\u2019t interact with sleepers with any regularity. Part of the cosmic horror of the Mythos is that the horrors that protagonists encounter don't only exist, but they are a fundamental part of our world. That strongly suggests to me that while some Mythos monsters may originate from the Abyss, the vast majority of them originate from the Fallen World, that is our material realm, The Shadow, The Astral, or The Underworld.<br /> <br /> (That said I often joke that Mastigos fight the Abyss by summoning Ringwraiths and the Hounds of Tindalos).<br /> <br /> Since dreams and the Dreamlands are so important to many stories in the Mythos cannon, that means many creatures may have connections the Astral. Perhaps the Denizens of Leng are specialized Goetia that have found a way to walk out of dreams and into reality? And do they have some connection with Beasts? The Idigam are already fully loaded for cosmic horrors from the dawn of time, but there have been references to stranger spirits from beyond the Lunar perimeter reaching Earth too. What happens when a spirit of light lands in a pack\u2019s territory if it originated near Carcoasa? The Underworld bears mentioning too, since the Chthonians are about as alien as you can get and are capable of wrecking havoc even before they pass through an Aventian Gate.<br /> <br /> Arcadia can\u2019t be overlooked either. I would be less willing to place Mythos characters there, although it can be done, as the Arkham Lost thread has shown us. That said, if stories can be told about it, you can find Changelings and the Wyrd in the mix. How exactly did the Hedge get changed by HPL and company?<br /> <br /> And finally, there is the terrifying, horrifying possibility that the Mythos monsters don\u2019t need to come from beyond, and that they already exist in the Material realm. The God-Machine is Lovecraftian enough already, no changes needed. Mummy, on the other hand, exists almost wholly in the Material Realm and has dropped hints of both Narlythotep and the King in Yellow.<br /> <br /> Fun times. Watch your Sanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 08-23-2016, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T14:43:46-07:00","id":956560,"title":"","content":"First things first: I wrote up modern Arkham as a Changeling 1e setting <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/168334-arkham-lost?p=956390#post956390\">here</a> and described Delta Green as a Hunter Compact <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/10139-compact-delta-green-the-organization\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Second things second: Years ago, I was one of many people working on a fangame that eventually failed called Outsider: the Calling, which was focused on normal human beings unwillingly warped by the Mythos and trying to figure out where to go from there, which in practice looked like a rough middle ground between Changeling and Deviant with a Lovecraftian coat of paint. While the rules were incredibly shoddy and the project stalled pretty quickly, you may want to skim through it; a quick Google search should pull it up.<br /> <br /> As for what already exists in the CofD that can be made Mythos-y (as opposed to pulling it in wholecloth to an admittedly crowded universe), you have quite a few options. Many of the heftier Mythos entities fit pretty well as Arcadian Keepers (imagine a musician like Eric Zahn dragged to the court of Azathoth to keep the blind idiot god asleep with unending music, or those called by dreams to serve Cthulhu who may eventually just wander into the surf im search of Rl'yeh) - and I think that's our easiest way in. There's a compelling argument to be made for Deep Ones and Mi-Go to be hobgoblins, I think, and that's to say nothing of how easily ghouls fit into Changeling as a race that wanders dreams with ease.<br /> <br /> While Mummy is ripe for this (as you mention, the Herald of Forgotten Stars and Ochre-Masked King are Nyarlathotep and Hastur in all but name), I feel like the Judges, demons, and black huriyah are all too remote from reality for use in the average CofD game by default. I'm all for making them less so, but that would require some doing to explain how they get out of Duat/the orbit of their dead stars.<br /> <br /> Mage is ripe with Lovecraftian potential, with the Temenos an easy analogue to the Dreamlands and the Abyss giving us gifts like sentient hostile alternate timelines. Some will argue that the Exarchs are Mythos critters, but I think they're too fundamentally tied into the humanist core of Awakening to fit that bill; the Great Old Ones don't care about oppressin mankind, they scarcely even notice it.<br /> <br /> God-Machine Angels are always a fun option for this sort of thing, but I think the qashmallim are much more terrifying because of their inscrutability; Angels serve the God-Machine, but qashmallim just act in accordance with the invisible whims of whatever the Divine Fire is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T14:56:29-07:00","id":956570,"title":"","content":"Huh, I didn't know you worked on Outsider. That cool! <br /> <br /> I like the idea of Azathoth as one of the True Fae, but I do have other way of looking at him in CofD that I'm quite fond of. It ties nicely with using Qashmallim as Mythos entities. The Principle is nothing less than the guiding light of Azathoth. Why does it drive Prometheans to become human? None can say, for who can know the will of the Blind Idiot God. Yet is is both the Flux and the Elipis, the Promethean and the Pandoran. It's purpose is contradictory, and in all likelihood unintentional in the creation of new life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:00:48-07:00","id":956573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=956570#post956570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I didn't know you worked on Outsider. That cool! <br /> <br /> I like the idea of Azathoth as one of the True Fae, but I do have other way of looking at him in CofD that I'm quite fond of. It ties nicely with using Qashmallim as Mythos entities. The Principle is nothing less than the guiding light of Azathoth. Why does it drive Prometheans to become human? None can say, for who can know the will of the Blind Idiot God. Yet is is both the Flux and the Elipis, the Promethean and the Pandoran. It's purpose is contradictory, and in all likelihood unintentional in the creation of new life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Azathoth-as-Divine Fire is a brilliant idea I hadn't considered. All the Divine Fire seemingly wants is change, and what is change if not chaos by a kinder name? The dichotomy of Elpis and Flux is an artificial divide enforced by a pathetic human mind trying to assign binary morality to something completely random, as we can see with the utterly alien actions of Arch-Qashmal. At best, the creation of new souls by the Divine Fire is a random positive side effect of this process and at worst its a means of creating new souls to enslave or devour.<br /> <br /> And of course, that's before we get into his title of &quot;Nuclear Chaos&quot; and what that means regarding the Zeky...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:09:53-07:00","id":956581,"title":"","content":"By the way, Second Chances, you really should check out Trail of Cthulhu if you haven't yet. While I mostly love it for the ruleset, many of the books and scenarios do very unique spins on some of the tired old Mythos critters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:16:55-07:00","id":956584,"title":"","content":"What with the Dreamlands being an important part of the Mythos... would you discount the possibility that the Great Old Ones could be particularly ancient Nightmares? And that any physical appearance of them is actually a Beast going Incarnate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:19:01-07:00","id":956586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=956584#post956584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What with the Dreamlands being an important part of the Mythos... would you discount the possibility that the Great Old Ones could be particularly ancient Nightmares? And that any physical appearance of them is actually a Beast going Incarnate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see that as similar to my description of the Exarchs above; Beasts are born from the incarnate fears of the human race while Lovecraft is all about the insignificance of mankind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:21:26-07:00","id":956587,"title":"","content":"Well, the Knights of St George and their Faceless Angels feels pretty Lovecraftian, and it won't be too hard to tie them to the Astral as a form of &quot;dreamlands&quot;. The Chtonian from the Underworld as dead gods which were never born or dead races of the Old Ones before humanity also has a great potential. The Brineborn from WAtP and the Drowned from SotUK are both great options to explore, IMO, together with how Fate from Mummy works as &quot;strange, cold stars from beyond earth&quot;. I'll be happy to contribute to the project, although my love for Lovecraft was pretty late to bloom (the first time I've heard about the Mythos was from the One Night at the Lonesome October, which is not that Lovecraftian, and I only understood things after reading Outsider: the Calling- but since discovering Eldritch Horror, I've pretty much fallen for the Mythos)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:22:11-07:00","id":956588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=956573#post956573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Azathoth-as-Divine Fire is a brilliant idea I hadn't considered. All the Divine Fire seemingly wants is change, and what is change if not chaos by a kinder name? The dichotomy of Elpis and Flux is an artificial divide enforced by a pathetic human mind trying to assign binary morality to something completely random, as we can see with the utterly alien actions of Arch-Qashmal. At best, the creation of new souls by the Divine Fire is a random positive side effect of this process and at worst its a means of creating new souls to enslave or devour.<br /> <br /> And of course, that's before we get into his title of &quot;Nuclear Chaos&quot; and what that means regarding the Zeky...</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right? I had a minor freakout when I put two and two together on that one. <br /> <br /> Your mention of dichotomy as being human constructs brings up a salient point about the Mythos though. They contradict each other all over the place, yet it still works. I see no reason why Azathoth-as-True Fae and Azathoth-as-Divine Fire can't coexist or even be the same being as Azathoth-as-Physical Star. These are things that are not meant to be know by human beings and they may very well be unknowable. Revel in the contradiction. <br /> <br /> Ditto goes for R'lyeh. It is important to me at least that the city be an physical place that anyone can enter without crossing realms if you can find it when it rises. Nothing stops you from stepping into it via dreams (the Astral) or hearing the Call and becoming entrapped in Arcadia/R'lyeh by a Fae-That-Is-Not-A-Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:36:41-07:00","id":956594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=956573#post956573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course, that's before we get into his title of &quot;Nuclear Chaos&quot; and what that means regarding the Zeky...</div> </div> </div> </div>That refers to him being the center of things, the nucleus, not nuclear as in nuclear energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:38:54-07:00","id":956596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=956594#post956594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That refers to him being the center of things, the nucleus, not nuclear as in nuclear energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of that, though later writers have ran with the atomic thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:50:01-07:00","id":956599,"title":"","content":"This has also highly influenced the way that I view Azathoth, even though it is definitely different from how HPL wrote him: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://lesswrong.com/lw/kr/an_alien_god/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/lesswrong-2-0/image/upload/v1654295382/new_mississippi_river_fjdmww.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://lesswrong.com/lw/kr/an_alien_god/\" target=\"_blank\"> An Alien God &mdash; LessWrong </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://lesswrong.com/lw/kr/an_alien_god/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://lesswrong.com/lw/kr/an_alien_god/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> \"A curious aspect of the theory of evolution,\" said Jacques Monod, \"is that everybody thinks he understands it.\" &hellip; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:11:26-07:00","id":956612,"title":"","content":"some more thoughts about Hunter-<br /> <br /> while the core mood of Hunter is not very Lovecraftian (it is more in the lines of &quot;I've just punched Cthulhu&quot;), the material itself could be refulffed to fit the setting. The Lucifuge, for example, could be a hybrid lineage of humans who carry the blood of a pre-human races. My Mythos lore is not that deep, so I'm not sure what could replace God/the Saints for the MM. The Director Board from Cheiron Group are mysterious enough to be connected to the Mythos, and the same applies for the Cainte Heresy. The Knights of St George I've already mentioned, and the Faithful of Shulpae would also have a nice lovecraftian feeling.<br /> <br /> That's what I have for the moment. Now- sleep :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:55:48-07:00","id":956629,"title":"","content":"Pangaeans fit the bill as it is. Considering what <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859687#post859687\">Harvest</a> looks like it's easy to imagine Shub-Niggurath as Reproduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-23-2016, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T17:33:58-07:00","id":956648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=956612#post956612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">some more thoughts about Hunter-<br /> <br /> while the core mood of Hunter is not very Lovecraftian (it is more in the lines of &quot;I've just punched Cthulhu&quot;), the material itself could be refulffed to fit the setting. The Lucifuge, for example, could be a hybrid lineage of humans who carry the blood of a pre-human races. My Mythos lore is not that deep, so I'm not sure what could replace God/the Saints for the MM. The Director Board from Cheiron Group are mysterious enough to be connected to the Mythos, and the same applies for the Cainte Heresy. The Knights of St George I've already mentioned, and the Faithful of Shulpae would also have a nice lovecraftian feeling.<br /> <br /> That's what I have for the moment. Now- sleep :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the only one of those that is really a refluff would be MM. The others can be worked into the Mythos fairly naturally. The Lucifage may not like finding out that they aren't the bloodline of fire and brimstone demons, but what can you do. Although, I think it works perfectly fine to have one group of the Lucifage be demon-blooded and another group be Deep One Hybrids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T03:24:28-07:00","id":956871,"title":"","content":"I think that correct way to go with Mythos in CoD universe is to analyze each Great Old One on it's own merits. Like I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895970-%E2%80%8B-2e-mystery-yellow-sign-hallows-network-corruption-and-abyssal-astral-realm\">King in Yellow and his Carcosa as Abyssal Anima Mundi Realm</a> of 'wrong' Atlantis.<br /> <br /> <b>As to Great Old Ones as Supernal beings - I do not think it works with basic premise.</b> Supernal Beings are 'perfect', but almost all Old Ones are somehow 'wrong' to reality, even if they are parts of it. They can work as various Lower Depths Realms emanations ( like Azathoth as True Fae ) or even Abyss corruptions of various elements of <b>CoD</b> reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T08:13:41-07:00","id":956974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=956648#post956648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the only one of those that is really a refluff would be MM. The others can be worked into the Mythos fairly naturally. The Lucifage may not like finding out that they aren't the bloodline of fire and brimstone demons, but what can you do. Although, I think it works perfectly fine to have one group of the Lucifage be demon-blooded and another group be Deep One Hybrids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, who says the Saint's Feast Days care about the calendar as opposed to about when certain Stars are Right? Just because they have ritual magic that works and gives them power and they <i>attribute</i> it to their god, doesn't mean it is that god that answers...<br /> <hr /><br /> Has anyone else read The Laundry series/books by Charles Stross?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T08:15:20-07:00","id":956976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=956871#post956871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>As to Great Old Ones as Supernal beings - I do not think it works with basic premise.</b> Supernal Beings are 'perfect', but almost all Old Ones are somehow 'wrong' to reality, even if they are parts of it. They can work as various Lower Depths Realms emanations ( like Azathoth as True Fae ) or even Abyss corruptions of various elements of <b>CoD</b> reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says they are &quot;wrong&quot;? Humans. That just means they are &quot;wrong&quot; to our perceptions of comfortable reality, not necessarily reality itself...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-24-2016, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:32:09-07:00","id":957157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=956976#post956976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says they are &quot;wrong&quot;? Humans. That just means they are &quot;wrong&quot; to our perceptions of comfortable reality, not necessarily reality itself...</div> </div> </div> </div>Reality. Or rather Quiescence. R'yleh is not more real than Atlantis. Carcosa is noting more than 'star-dream' incarnation.<br /> <br /> Also, modern CoD universe is ruled by Exarchs. They <i>are </i>on the Thrones of Reality. <b>Great Old Ones <i>can</i> be Old Gods of previous realities, but surely not this one.</b><br /> <br /> Also remember one thing - Old Ones are <u>beings</u>. They are not 'gods' in terms we understand it. Cthulhu is still just giant squid with tentacles - he have magical powers, is colossal in size. But it's still <i>'only'</i> creature, not proper reality remaking god.<br /> <br /> Gods are Exarchs. Great Old Ones - at least to Lovecraft - are only 'supermonsters'.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:13:36-07:00","id":957180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=957157#post957157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reality. Or rather Quiescence. R'yleh is not more real than Atlantis. Carcosa is noting more than 'star-dream' incarnation.<br /> <br /> Also, modern CoD universe is ruled by Exarchs. They <i>are </i>on the Thrones of Reality. <b>Great Old Ones <i>can</i> be Old Gods of previous realities, but surely not this one.</b><br /> <br /> Also remember one thing - Old Ones are <u>beings</u>. They are not 'gods' in terms we understand it. Cthulhu is still just giant squid with tentacles - he have magical powers, is colossal in size. But it's still <i>'only'</i> creature, not proper reality remaking god.<br /> <br /> Gods are Exarchs. Great Old Ones - at least to Lovecraft - are only 'supermonsters'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quiescence covers the Supernal. What happens when Sleepers witness the Supernal? Their minds break. What happens when people witness the Great Old Ones? Their minds break.<br /> <br /> Who says Atlantis <i>wasn't</i> R'yleh? Not the Mage Chroniclers Guide at the very least.<br /> <br /> And who says the Outer Gods don't strike fear into the Exarchs? Or that Exarchs aren't the mere dreaming fragments of Outer Gods? But Cthulhu <i>was</i> only a high priest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:18:09-07:00","id":957182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=957180#post957180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quiescence covers the Supernal. What happens when Sleepers witness the Supernal? Their minds break. What happens when people witness the Great Old Ones? Their minds break.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, minds of Sleepers break when witnessing non-Supernal magic as well.<br /> <br /> But yeah, when it comes to the Exarchs they are supermonsters-as-gods. While I don't believe they would fit as Supernal beings for a variety of other reasons, them being 'supermonsters' isn't one of them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T00:28:20-07:00","id":957445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=957182#post957182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, when it comes to the Exarchs they are supermonsters-as-gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Exarchs are <i><b>humans</b>-turned-into-gods</i> - that they are now have traits of 'supermonsters' is just side effect of their Ascension. Remember that now days CoD universe is <i>humancentric</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Cthulhu and company are 'just' supermonsters - they maybe are once Supernal Realms Old Gods, but they Fallen into our reality and are just super powerful monsters/phenomena.</b> I could ascribe to this paradigm as it has most sense with both Mythos and CoD universe lore.<br /> <br /> Remember, Great Old Ones are <i>less</i> powerful than <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Outer_Gods\" target=\"_blank\">Outer Gods</a>. To be faithfull to Mythos, you need to make Great Old Ones as category <i>lower </i>to most powerful beings in reality. Intereting would be making Exarchs equal with Outer Gods... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>www.yog-sothoth.com</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">An <b>Outer God</b> is a fictional deity in the <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Cthulhu_mythos\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu mythos</a> of <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/H.P._Lovecraft\" target=\"_blank\">H.P. Lovecraft</a>. Unlike the <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Great_Old_Ones_(Deities)\" target=\"_blank\">Great Old Ones</a>, the Outer Gods are vastly more powerful and function on a cosmic scale. Although the distinction between the two groups has been recognized by some mythos authors, it was the <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Role-playing_game\" target=\"_blank\">role-playing game</a> <i><a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Call_of_Cthulhu_role-playing_game\" target=\"_blank\">Call of Cthulhu</a></i> that first introduced the term &quot;Outer Gods&quot;. Nonetheless, the delineation between the <i>Outer Gods</i> and the <i>Great Old Ones</i> is not always clear, and some scholars do not recognize the distinction at all.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">According to <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/H.P._Lovecraft\" target=\"_blank\">H.P. Lovecraft</a>'s cosmology, there are two sets of Outer Gods: the <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Elder_God_(Cthulhu_mythos)\" target=\"_blank\">Elder Gods</a> and the <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Great_Ones\" target=\"_blank\">Other Gods</a>. Though the terms &quot;Outer Gods&quot; and &quot;Other Gods&quot; are often mistakenly used interchageably, the beings decribed below are the Outer Gods. The Outer Gods are &quot;mindless blasphemies&quot; from outside the capacity of humanity to understand. Most of the time, they are asleep and/or insane, and would like to see humanity dead, devoured, or made slaves. They include <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Azathoth\" target=\"_blank\">Azathoth</a>, <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Nyarlathotep\" target=\"_blank\">Nyarlathotep</a>, and <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Shub-Niggurath\" target=\"_blank\">Shub-Niggurath</a>. The Elder Gods are presumed to be good, but are distant and unmoved by humanities cries. Periodically, they may be invoked, but they generally neglect humanity, leaving them in the hands of the Outer Gods.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T00:30:20-07:00","id":957447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=957182#post957182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, when it comes to the Exarchs they are supermonsters-as-gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Exarchs are <i><b>humans</b>-turned-into-gods</i> - that they are now have traits of 'supermonsters' is just side effect of their Ascension. Remember that now days CoD universe is <i>humancentric</i>. <br /> <br /> <b>Cthulhu and company are 'just' supermonsters - they maybe are once Supernal Realms Old Gods, but they Fallen into our reality and are just super powerful monsters/phenomena.</b> I could ascribe to this paradigm as it has most sense with both Mythos and CoD universe lore.<br /> <br /> Remember, Great Old Ones are <i>less</i> powerful than <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Outer_Gods\" target=\"_blank\">Outer Gods</a>. To be faithfull to Mythos, you need to make Great Old Ones as category <i>lower </i>to most powerful beings in reality. Intereting would be making Exarchs equal with Outer Gods... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yog-Sothoth Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">An <b>Outer God</b> is a fictional deity in the <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Cthulhu_mythos\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu mythos</a> of <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/H.P._Lovecraft\" target=\"_blank\">H.P. Lovecraft</a>. Unlike the <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Great_Old_Ones_(Deities)\" target=\"_blank\">Great Old Ones</a>, the Outer Gods are vastly more powerful and function on a cosmic scale. (...) Nonetheless, the delineation between the <i>Outer Gods</i> and the <i>Great Old Ones</i> is not always clear, and some scholars do not recognize the distinction at all.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">According to <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/H.P._Lovecraft\" target=\"_blank\">H.P. Lovecraft</a>'s cosmology, there are two sets of Outer Gods: the <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Elder_God_(Cthulhu_mythos)\" target=\"_blank\">Elder Gods</a> and the <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Great_Ones\" target=\"_blank\">Other Gods</a>. Though the terms &quot;Outer Gods&quot; and &quot;Other Gods&quot; are often mistakenly used interchageably, the beings decribed below are the Outer Gods. The Outer Gods are &quot;mindless blasphemies&quot; from outside the capacity of humanity to understand. Most of the time, they are asleep and/or insane, and would like to see humanity dead, devoured, or made slaves. They include <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Azathoth\" target=\"_blank\">Azathoth</a>, <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Nyarlathotep\" target=\"_blank\">Nyarlathotep</a>, and <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Shub-Niggurath\" target=\"_blank\">Shub-Niggurath</a>. The Elder Gods are presumed to be good, but are distant and unmoved by humanities cries. Periodically, they may be invoked, but they generally neglect humanity, leaving them in the hands of the Outer Gods.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T00:41:16-07:00","id":957450,"title":"","content":"Simple analogy is using Ancient Greece Mythology:<br /> <br /> <i>If Great Old Ones are Titans, Outer Gods are Olympics Gods. </i><br /> <br /> <b>Putting this on CoD universe, if Outer Gods are Exarchs, then Great Old Ones are Old Gods of Supernal, fallen on Earth, when Exarchs took their Thrones.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:22:25-07:00","id":957559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=957447#post957447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, Exarchs are <i><b>humans</b>-turned-into-gods</i> - that they are now have traits of 'supermonsters' is just side effect of their Ascension. Remember that now days CoD universe is <i>humancentric</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Cthulhu and company are 'just' supermonsters - they maybe are once Supernal Realms Old Gods, but they Fallen into our reality and are just super powerful monsters/phenomena.</b> I could ascribe to this paradigm as it has most sense with both Mythos and CoD universe lore.<br /> <br /> Remember, Great Old Ones are <i>less</i> powerful than <a href=\"http://www.yog-sothoth.com/wiki/index.php/Outer_Gods\" target=\"_blank\">Outer Gods</a>. To be faithfull to Mythos, you need to make Great Old Ones as category <i>lower </i>to most powerful beings in reality. Intereting would be making Exarchs equal with Outer Gods... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just to play Devil's advocate here, what if the Exarch's don't have as firm of a grip on reality as they pretend? Maybe they drove out a majority of the Old Gods and control a large portion of the Supernal, but some powerful Old Gods managed to hold onto their position, and sometimes, for their own inscrutable reasons, they reach out to influence the Phenomenal World much like the Exarch's communicate with their servants and manifest Ochemeta?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, maybe some beings come from distant stars by worming their way through secret paths that few others know about in the Sidereal Wastes? Maybe Carcosa actually can be found on a planet orbiting Aldebaran? Or maybe they are beings native to an alien Temenos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:36:28-07:00","id":957634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=957447#post957447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Exarchs are <i><b>humans</b>-turned-into-gods</i> - that they are now have traits of 'supermonsters' is just side effect of their Ascension. Remember that now days CoD universe is <i>humancentric</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/503363-exarchs-as-nonhumans\">They aren't necessarily humans-turned-into-gods</a>, whether or not you think the CoD universe is humancentric. If the Lie is something that can be overcome, and Awakening suggests it might be, then it's possible the Exarchs are just your 'supermonsters' who have a really good con going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:02:27-07:00","id":957681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=957450#post957450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple analogy is using Ancient Greece Mythology:<br /> <br /> <i>If Great Old Ones are Titans, Outer Gods are Olympics Gods. </i><br /> <br /> <b>Putting this on CoD universe, if Outer Gods are Exarchs, then Great Old Ones are Old Gods of Supernal, fallen on Earth, when Exarchs took their Thrones.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That analogy doesn't neccesarily follow, the Titans were the generation elder to the Olympians and easily on par with their power, whereas the Great Old Ones have sometimes been described as the priests of the Outer Gods.<br /> <br /> It should also be pointed out that the Mythos is by its nature collaborative and contradictory. Interpreting the Outer Gods and/or Great Old Ones as &quot;supermonsters&quot; works for some people. Interpreting them as literal gods works for others, and other RPGs have done so. Given the aforementioned collaborative-contradictory nature of the Mythos, the stuff that Chaosium, Pagan Publishing, Final Fantasy, and Paizo have created is just as up for discussion as any other author. We can each then pick and choose what we want to use at our tables. Trying to determine who is &quot;correct&quot; in their interpretation is likely an excercise in futility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:12:31-07:00","id":957686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=957681#post957681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can each then pick and choose what we want to use at our tables. Trying to determine who is &quot;correct&quot; in their interpretation is likely an excercise in futility.</div> </div> </div> </div>We still need to agree on some general model if fan book is to come. Are we making them all one kind of fenomena or various diffrent things? Like with Azathoth as Divine Fire and Carcosa as Abyssal Anima Mundi Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:16:12-07:00","id":957688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=957686#post957686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We still need to agree on some general model if fan book is to come. Are we making them all one kind of fenomena or various diffrent things? Like with Azathoth as Divine Fire and Carcosa as Abyssal Anima Mundi Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is a fanbook coming out of Age of Azar or the Sundered World threads? I made this topic as a place for discussion and centralization if other threads spawn from it. Trying to create a fan book is far too ambitious in my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[R