ttps://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:12:24-07:00","id":957962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=957764#post957764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what are doing here? Cause without some fan material as goal all the talk is going to be 'at my table it will be this and that...'</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote an entire city with new Kiths /and/ a Hunter Compact! Is that not enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T20:25:57-07:00","id":958026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=957962#post957962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wrote an entire city with new Kiths /and/ a Hunter Compact! Is that not enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me, I need to link to those in the first post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T22:15:02-07:00","id":958063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=957962#post957962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote an entire city with new Kiths /and/ a Hunter Compact! Is that not enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>really </i>appreciate your work on Arkham, but what does it give STs wanting to run Mortal game about Mythos? They will not grab <b>Changeling</b> rules for this for sure. They could use Compact, but then it will be <b>Hunter</b> game. What about ST wanting to run Mysthos stories in <b>Mage</b>? In <b>Werewolf</b>?<br /> <br /> If you make topic like 'Mythos Chronicles' I assumed it was next try at fan book, akin to what <b>Inferno</b> is to demons lore.<br /> <br /> There are here good ideas, I just think something more than 'at my table we do this and that' to come. God dammit, we have whole fan book on <b>Silent Hill</b>, don't we!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T23:21:47-07:00","id":958079,"title":"","content":"For a fan book similar to <b>Inferno</b>, I would propose this kind of schema:<ul><li><b>Introduction</b></li> <li><b>Chapter 1: Mythos</b> \u2013 Various theories on nature of Mythos creature. Two or three main models. Skill <i>Occult (Mythos)</i> write up. Basic Integrity mechanics on contacts with Mythos creature \u2013 probably some general penalties and new Condition or two. Thinking if some Ephemeral Beings rules need to be added.</li> <li><b>Chapter 2: Strange Aeons </b>\u2013 History of Mythos studies with some plot hooks</li> <li><b>Chapter 3: Stars are Right </b>\u2013 Rules and theories to use Mythos with supernatural, like Azatoth as True Fae or Divine Fire.</li> <li><b>Chapter 4: Legions of Madness</b> - stats for few Servitor Races, probably as Horrors from <b>CoD</b> rulebook.</li> <li><b>Chapter 5: Arkham</b> - With permission of <b>atamajakki</b>, would add and expand on Arkham material for <b>CoD</b> setting of it.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T00:32:10-07:00","id":958089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956545-open-call-the-mythos-chronicles?p=958079#post958079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a fan book similar to <b>Inferno</b>, I would propose this kind of schema:<ul><li><b>Introduction</b></li> <li><b>Chapter 1: Mythos</b> \u2013 Various theories on nature of Mythos creature. Two or three main models. Skill <i>Occult (Mythos)</i> write up. Basic Integrity mechanics on contacts with Mythos creature \u2013 probably some general penalties and new Condition or two. Thinking if some Ephemeral Beings rules need to be added.</li> <li><b>Chapter 2: Strange Aeons </b>\u2013 History of Mythos studies with some plot hooks</li> <li><b>Chapter 3: Stars are Right </b>\u2013 Rules and theories to use Mythos with supernatural, like Azatoth as True Fae or Divine Fire.</li> <li><b>Chapter 4: Legions of Madness</b> - stats for few Servitor Races, probably as Horrors from <b>CoD</b> rulebook.</li> <li><b>Chapter 5: Arkham</b> - With permission of <b>atamajakki</b>, would add and expand on Arkham material for <b>CoD</b> setting of it.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds pretty good to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T10:20:42-07:00","id":958788,"title":"","content":"I have a different take on Changeling Lovecraftian horror then Arkham Lost.<br /> <br /> I'm less directly imposing a Lovecraftian elements, like the town of Arkham, and more about adding elemental of alien, unknowable horror to Changeling, so when I say Lovecraftian I mean the Genre, not specific Lovecraftian elements (although Arkham Lost is very cool).<br /> <br /> What I mean is the True Fae are horrifying, alien beings that are so toxic and alien to relatity that not only can they not normally exist in it, they can't understand it well enough to interact with it.<br /> <br /> So a alien horror goes to Arcadia and wraps makes a deal with the wyrd, is given a name and titles and wraps itself in glamour.<br /> <br /> So the titles allow this...thing to interact with Arcadia and the Hedge and Iron side.<br /> <br /> And most beings are dealing with this fairy fascade having no idea that its just a faberication. <br /> <br /> So sometimes the fact that the True Fae do weird things or come off a being odd, its because the\u2019re alien horrors at the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T11:05:37-07:00","id":958810,"title":"","content":"The True Fae cloth themselves story and folk tales and dreams, because its them an interface with reality.<br /> <br /> Most beings dealing with them will see and understand them via the manifestations of their names and titles, but if they dig deeper, do research in the stranger places and they learn to look beyond the titles and names, they'll see a horror existing in dimesions beyond human keen, shifting between shapes the refuse to obey all limitations of geometry, and colours that exist in isolation from any in the light spectrum, yet seething it a life that violates even the most warped forms of the natural life cycle.<br /> <br /> House rule anyone who looked at the alien &quot;soul&quot; of a seemingly fae &quot;True&quot; Fae, has to roll for clarity every day until the memory is stripped from their minds.<br /> <br /> Under Little Red Riding Hoods cloak beats the soul something that wears her like a skin, so thing so warped and pulsating that the minds is crushed under the weight of its Alieness, if one finds away to get a glimpse of its true nature.<br /> <br /> The True Fae do not encourage this, they do not want to be reminded if their true selves, they prefer the comfortable fairy tales, for after all these millienia, the truth dusturbs even them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:06:33-07:00","id":963281,"title":"","content":"My gift to project - Hastur ( in two avatars ) and his servitors for <b>CoD</b> games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895970-\u200b-2e-mystery-yellow-sign-hallows-network-corruption-and-abyssal-astral-realm?p=963000#post963000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I ran whole plot with created beings to it, here are NPCs for the Mystery. There are two kinds, both in Abyssal versions. Goetia are Astral archetypes and 'demons of mind'. Horrors are 'physical' beings, rules for them are in <b>CoD</b> Rulebook - but those particular are ones from Anima Mundi Realm of Carcosa. King in Yellow is more from nightmares and dreams than body flesh, but Feaster from Afar is physical only in Carcossa. As both Avatars of Hastur, you can change King in Yellow into Feaster from Afar, or vice versa. Treat yourself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Warning:</b> Fight with King almost beat my high ranking mages test cabal with Abyssal specialists - 10 Awakened, Gnosis 5-6, Masters or Double Adepts, 5 of them from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/915818-2e-fan-choir-of-hashmallim\">Choir of Hashmallim</a>. By the end of of it, they were with <i>no</i> Mana. <u><i>Do not </i></u>throw Avatars of Madness as direct threat if you are not sure your PCs can handel it.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/gWK5SLn.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Name: </b>King in Yellow ( Hastur ) <b>Type:</b> Abyssal Goetia<br /> <b>Rank: </b>5 ( Avatar of Rank 6 entity - Carcosa ) <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <br /> <b>Power:</b> 15 <b>Finesses:</b> 11 <b>Resistance:</b> 13 <b>Essence:</b> 50/50<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 18 <b>Willpower:</b> 10 <b>Initiative:</b> 26 <b>Defense:</b> 11 <b>Speed:</b> 31<br /> <br /> <b>Influences:</b> Madness 5, Paradox 5 <b>Manifestations:</b> 5 to choose, thought about Posses<br /> <br /> <b>Numina: </b><ul><li><b>Unbreakable</b></li> </ul>The creature is nearly indestructible. Any attack that does not score an exceptional success inflicts only a single point of bashing damage. Exceptional successes inflict damage as normal. If the creature has a weakness of some sort, attacks incorporating that weakness bypass this power.<ul><li><b>Resistant </b>by me</li> </ul>Entity resist Supernal Magic much more efficiently than other of her kind \u2013 she get\u2019s automatic Withstand source equal to its Rank against Awakened spells. That means she generally have Rank+1 Withstand, as its Attributes are normal source of Withstand, see rules of Withstanding, <b>MtAw</b> 2E page 114.<ul><li><b>Flesh of Abyss</b> by me ( idea from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\">amechra</a> )</li> </ul>Entity is build from the stuff of Abyss itself. That means, Supernal Magic have really harder time to interact with it. Each spell cast on entity is treated as one Spell Factor lower \u2013 that means that attack spells makes one damage lower, Scale is treated as needing to get Size 6 to work on it and Duration is shorter than caster imagined when making Imago.<ul><li><b>Copies</b> by me</li> </ul>The entity is \u2018one in many\u2019. She can make copies of herself, working like effects of <i>Manifold Presence</i> spell, giving many possible instances of it. They all are connected to proper entity, but not so hurting. Each copy can be destroyed with full Bashing damage of Corpus from main entity and takes one Willpower from entity pool. Each copy is treated as entity itself for using it\u2019s powers or targeting it\u2019s targets.<ul><li><b>Paradox Gorging</b> by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\">GibberingEloquence</a><br /> The entity reflexively rolls Resistance + Rank whenever Paradox is incurred in its presence. Each Success heals 1 lethal or bashing damage, and 3 Successes heals 1 aggravated damage. They may use their Influence over Paradoxes in conjunction with this Aspect and Numina to keep healing every turn. Paradox Gorging let's an Abyssal reflexively eat another of equal or lesser Rank by spending 1 willpower point and rolling Power + Rank vs Resistance + Rank. Success destroys the target Abyssal, and the gorging entity heals [the target's Rank x 2] in any type of damage.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Presence of Paradox</b> by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\">amechra</a><br /> The ephemeral being is thoroughly tainted by the stuff of the Abyss - treat it as if it were an entire crowd of Sleepers for the purposes of calculating Paradox dice pools, except it adds dice equal to its Rank rather than just one. In addition, it may spend Essence reflexively to cancel Mana spent to mitigate a Paradox dice pool on a one-to-one basis.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Madness</b></li> </ul>Anyone seeing Hastur need to roll Composure + Supernatural Advantage each turn, or they will go mad. Mind Shield spell makes it Clash of Wills on Gnosis + Mind of caster. On losing, victim makes any commands of Hastur and recite damn verses of theatrical play.<ul><li><b>Summoning</b></li> </ul>King in Yellow can summon Rank 1-3 Abyssal Goetia beings spending 1 Essence for each in Carcosa.<ul><li><b>Blast</b></li> </ul>Projection of mind braking insanity \u2013 works as from <b>CoD </b>Rulebook.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/X3tX5Sj.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <i>\u201cHe felt it coming. The air grew frigid, as if it blew out of the black interstices of interstellar space\u2026 It glided down out of the icy sky like the \ufb01nal concentrated essence of all nonhuman horror. It was black, in\ufb01nitely old, shriveled and humped like some kind of enormous air-borne monkey. A kind of iridescence played about it and its \ufb01xed blazing eyes were of no color known on earth\u2026 As it grew close to the knoll, it extended appendages, which resembled tentacles, tipped with knifelike talons.\u201d</i><br /> \u2013Joseph Payne Brennan, <i>\u201cThe Feaster from Afar\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <b>Name: </b> The Feaster from Afar ( Hastur ) <b>Type:</b> Abyssal Horror <b>Potency: </b>9 <b>Size:</b> 25<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 6<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 9, Dexterity 7, Stamina 10<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 7, Manipulation 3, Composure 1<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Occult 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 4, Brawl 5, Survival 3, Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Intimidation 4, Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Hardy \u2022\u2022\u2022, Iron Stamina \u2022\u2022\u2022, Relentless \u2022\u2022, Iron Will \u2022\u2022, Grappling \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Flying, Unbreakable, Resistant, Flesh of Abyss, Paradox Gorging, Natural Weapons \u2022\u2022\u2022 (Tentacles), Multi-Attack \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Freighting, Armor ( Potency/2)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 16<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Hungry<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> To devour lives. Sate hunger.<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Health: </b>35<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 4/0<ul><li><b>Multi-Attack</b> \u2013 Can attack extra time up to dots. ( Feaster can make up to 5 attacks in round because of his multiple heads. )</li> <li><b>Freighting - </b>Anyone seeing Hastur need to roll Resolve + Composure each turn, or they will run for their lives. Mind Shield spell makes it Clash of Wills on Gnosis + Mind of caster. On losing, victim makes run as fast as it can from Hastur.</li> </ul><b>Weapons/Attacks:</b><br /> <b>Type Damage Range Dice Pool</b><br /> Tentacle and Biting 3L Melee 14<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Name: </b>\u2018Flat\u2019 Shadows <b>Type:</b> Abyssal Goetia <b>Rank: </b>2 <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <br /> <b>Power:</b> 4 <b>Finesses:</b> 4 <b>Resistance:</b> 3 <b>Essence:</b> 15/15<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 8 <b>Willpower:</b> 7 <b>Initiative:</b> 26 <b>Defense:</b> 11 <b>Speed:</b> 31<br /> <br /> <b>Influences:</b> Spatial 2, Paradox 2 <b>Manifestations:</b> 2<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Flesh of Abyss, Presence of Paradox , Flattening<ul><li><b>Flattening</b> by me</li> </ul>Being can make 3D being into 2D beings image, that is also living. He need to win Grapple Contest and spend 1 Willpower.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/rGcYmpV.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Name: </b>Byakhee <b>Type:</b> Abyssal Horror <b>Potency:</b> 3 <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Investigation 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Survival 2<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Intimidation 3, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Flying, Flesh of Abyss, Natural Weapons \u2022\u2022 ( Claws and Biting ), Armor ( Potency/2)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Obeying<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Hungry<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> To devour lives. To travel outside of space<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Health: </b>8<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1/0<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks:</b><br /> <b>Type Damage Range Dice Pool</b><br /> Claws 1L Melee 8<br /> Biting 2L Melee 8</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T16:02:34-07:00","id":963427,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it was covered by one of my questions is, how would the sanity points be calculated? Would it just be based off of Integrity or something else? What could constitute as testing your sanity? Would reading from the Necromonicon require you to role 2 dice if it was based on Integrity? How would spells be handled? I'm also curious as to how Hunter, Vampire, or Geist be handled in the Call of Cthulhu universe since most of them have supernatural powers, isn't the purpose of an H.P. Lovecraft game to encounter something that is beyond your perception of real until you die or go insane? I would think the game would be a very short one if it was based on Integrity rolls, if I'm mistaken please let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10133-yarrumkin","name":"Yarrumkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10133_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T23:04:45-07:00","id":963563,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10133-yarrumkin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10133_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10133\" data-vbnamecard=\"10133\">Yarrumkin</a> first you should answer yourself what you actually want to do - Mythos elements in <b>CoD</b> games, or Call of Cthulhu with adding supernaturals? This particular topic is for first, so we only add Mythos to all working <b>CoD </b>games.<br /> <br /> In this light, Sanity mechanics are redundant - they are clogged, based on d100 and, most important, Integrity measure more or less the same ( mental trauma ). I <i>will </i>write Mythos based Integrity rules in spare time. If you have ideas on suitable 'Resolution' Conditions, I'm all ears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}